What is Urea Fertilizer?
Urea fertilizer is a nitrogen rich synthetic compound that contains approximately 46 % nitrogen by weight. It is produced by reacting ammonia with carbon dioxide under high pressure, yielding white crystalline granules or prills that can be applied via broadcasting, fertigation, or foliar spraying. Because of its high nitrogen concentration, low cost per unit of nitrogen, and ease of handling, urea remains the most widely used nitrogen source in modern agriculture.
